' 11. Report a learner → admin resolves
' Use cases: Report a learner (Friends & communicate) + Review reports (Manage users) · Actors: Learner, Admin
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Unit of work: resolving (outcome, warning, suspension, replies to every reporter, closing their requests,
'     audit log entry) is one transaction (services/moderation.service.ts)
'   - Observer: every reporter (and a warned learner) gets the reply in their open tabs via publish()
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate → requireAdmin on the admin routes
'   - Repository
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 11 Report and resolve
title 11. Report a learner → admin resolves
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "Friend controller" as FCtrl
control "Moderation\nservice" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Live updates\n(RealtimeBus)" as Bus
boundary "Admin web app" as AdminWeb
actor Admin

Learner -> Web : Report B (from B's profile), reason
Web -> FCtrl : POST /api/people/:username/report
FCtrl -> Svc : reportLearner()
Svc -> Repo : reason given? under 10 reports a day?
alt an open report by this learner about B exists
  Svc -> Repo : add to that support request
else
  Svc -> Repo : new support request + report
end
Repo -> DB : INSERT …
FCtrl --> Web : "Report sent"

Admin -> AdminWeb : open Reports
AdminWeb -> Svc : GET /api/admin/reports
note over AdminWeb, Svc : «Chain of responsibility»: authenticate → requireAdmin
Svc -> Repo : open reports grouped per learner
Svc --> AdminWeb : groups (flagged when 3+ learners report)
Admin -> AdminWeb : choose an outcome
AdminWeb -> Svc : POST /api/admin/reports/:userId/resolve
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  alt dismiss
    Svc -> Repo : mark reports dismissed
  else warn
    Svc -> Repo : warning to B as a support message
  else suspend
    Svc -> Repo : B's account suspended (token version + 1)
  end
  Svc -> Repo : reply to every reporter, close their requests
  Svc -> Repo : audit log entry
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE / INSERT …
end
Svc -> Bus : publish(reporters, "inbox")
note right of Bus : «Observer»
Bus --> Web : reply appears in Help & support
Svc --> AdminWeb : resolved
@enduml
